A `--target` that names nothing on disk is not an error: the machine reports `not-started` with the
synthetic bootstrap edge, exactly as a missing declared artifact does, at exit 0.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-run
title: Run
summary: Single-machine fixture for playbook-state.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []
  research: [intake]

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: researching
            when: intake complete
            gates: ["request captured in the artifact"]
          - to: parked
            when: the run is shelved
      researching:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: research complete
      parked: {terminal: true}
      done: {terminal: true}
